      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. The actual test method `test_Chronology_range` is compact and focused, but the file has a huge number of unused imports and data provider methods that don't belong to this test. I'll clean it up significantly.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version removes ~180 lines of unused data provider methods and irrelevant imports, keeping only the 6 imports and 1 assertion framework import needed by the test. A Javadoc comment explains why each field's range is non-trivial (particularly the cutover year 1752 context), and inline comments on each assertion clarify the rationale."
